# Dark field, accent pop

**Tier 2 — the current field recipe** (`design/DESIGN-AUTHORITY.md`). Mandatory in Maintenance Mode. In Exploration Mode it is the benchmark a concept is measured against, not a boundary: a concept may propose a different field/contrast model if it says why and still reads as premium, precise and cybersecurity-first (Tier 1). The "Do not" list at the bottom records directions that failed in this system; a concept that revisits one must answer the reason it failed.

Vibrant color pops **because** the field is black/charcoal and quiet — not because boxes are filled with purple.

## Background ladder (2–3 steps)

OpenMSP’s move is juxtaposition of a few dark values — page black, a slightly lighter rounded section box, darker inset cards. Map that recipe to DE tokens. Do **not** adopt their yellow, numerals, Slack magenta, or layout.

| Step | OpenMSP (reference only) | DE token | Use |
|------|--------------------------|----------|-----|
| Canvas / well | `#161616` | `--de-bg` `#050312` (html gutters `#000`) | Page field; inset cards inside a style box |
| Style box | `#212121` | `--de-raised` `#151217` + `--de-hairline` | Contained chapter box — **2–4 flat chapters max** |
| Full-bleed chapter | — | `--de-surface` `#0a0a0a` | Adjacent dark chapter that stays a slab |
| Pop | their yellow — do not copy | `#D3126A` | CTA fill, active border, colon, icon |

Violet `#5B45E0` / `#8B5CF6` = lighting only. Never a wash fill.

**Yellow verdict:** the DE wordmark is white; the 3-bar mark is gold (`#e7b20d` / `#f5e48a`). That gold is a *secondary* mark color. It does **not** replace magenta. Do not use OpenMSP yellow (`#ffbe0b`) as a brand color or CTA fill. Do not paint numerals yellow.

**Midpoint:** if a chapter already reads well, leave it or make a one-step field shift (well ↔ surface). Do not wrap every homepage section in a rounded gray island. Hero stays atmospheric. Paper stays paper.

## Recipe (DE tokens only)

| Role | Token | Use |
|------|--------|-----|
| Deep well | `--de-bg` `#050312` | Page / chapter field / inset cards |
| Marketing field | `--de-surface` `#0a0a0a` | Adjacent dark chapter |
| Style box / raised | `--de-raised` `#151217` + `--de-hairline` | Contained chapter box, panels, chips |
| Pop | `#D3126A` | CTA fill, active border, colon, icon |

## Do

- Black/charcoal field → charcoal style box → inset `--de-bg` cards → white type → magenta punctuation
- Hairline chips: transparent/`bg-de-raised`, `border-de-hairline`; active = `border-[#D3126A]`
- Magenta colon after a statement heading (Trust / Engage pattern)
- Paper chapters: white lift + magenta accent, not violet-100 fills
- Utility: `.de-style-box` / `.de-style-box-inset` in `index.css`

## Do not

- Purple/navy/indigo fills on cards, chips, buttons, or section backgrounds
- `bg-violet-500/15`, `from-purple-600 to-indigo-600`, `#FF00FF`, rainbow
- Glass `bg-white/5 backdrop-blur` as the card recipe
- Giant neon blooms or cyberpunk glow
- Copy OpenMSP/OpenFrame logos, copy, yellow buttons, yellow numerals, APPROVE/REJECT, or fake “Featured in”
- Turn every chapter into a big rounded gray container

```tsx
// ❌ muddy chrome
<div className="rounded-2xl bg-violet-500/15 backdrop-blur-xl">
  <span className="bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-600 to-indigo-600">CTA</span>
</div>

// ✅ quiet field, accent pops
<div className="rounded-2xl border border-de-hairline bg-de-raised">
  <span className="bg-[#D3126A] text-white">Get My Cyber Risk Assessment</span>
</div>
```
